# Force LF line endings, needed for Docker to work on Windows
*.sh text eol=lf

# The bibliography is generated by bin/sync-sot.ps1, copied from a source that lives
# outside this repository and uses LF. On Windows, git's autocrlf would hand the working
# tree a CRLF copy on checkout — and the next sync would then see a file that differs
# from its source, rewrite it back to LF, and leave a modification that never goes away.
# The result is a permanently dirty file whose diffs mean nothing, on the one file where
# a diff must always mean something. Keep it LF on both sides.
*.bib text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the sync scripts themselves: sync-sot.ps1 must stay pure ASCII with
# stable line endings, because Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a BOM-less .ps1 as ANSI.
bin/*.ps1 text eol=lf

# The CV is a generated PDF copied in by the same script. Mark it binary explicitly so no
# line-ending or diff heuristic can ever touch it.
*.pdf binary

# _data/profile.yml and _data/socials.yml are generated the same way and must match what a
# checkout produces, or every clone would show them as modified straight away.
_data/*.yml text eol=lf
